            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for sharing!\r\n\r\nI believe there is a loose `vim.fn.strchars(reg_contents)` call in the original code that does nothing.\r\n\r\nBut of course my suggestion would be to get comfortable with `<C-r>` to paste from register and `+` as system register. This will come in handy in various situations. For example, I find myself using `\"+gr` with 'mini.operators' `replace` operator quite a lot.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks for sharing!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I believe there is a loose <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.fn.strchars(reg_contents)</code> call in the original code that does nothing.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But of course my suggestion would be to get comfortable with <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-r&gt;</code> to paste from register and <code class=\"notranslate\">+</code> as system register. This will come in handy in various situations. For example, I find myself using <code class=\"notranslate\">\"+gr</code> with 'mini.operators' <code class=\"notranslate\">replace</code> operator quite a lot.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Thanks for sharing!\nI believe there is a loose vim.fn.strchars(reg_contents) call in the original code that does nothing.\nBut of course my suggestion would be to get comfortable with <C-r> to paste from register and + as system register. This will come in handy in various situations. For example, I find myself using \"+gr with 'mini.operators' replace operator quite a lot.",
